{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8b7e4a02-9f2d-4f3b-9b6a-microservicesk8s",
    "name": "microservices-k8s (Spring Boot, 5 services)",
    "description": "End-to-end coverage against the API Gateway with the standard response envelope.\n\nResponse shape (all endpoints):\n{\n  \"code\": \"<http-status-as-string>\",\n  \"data\": <payload or null>,\n  \"message\": \"<human-readable>\",\n  \"pagination\": { \"page\": 1, \"size\": N, \"total_counts\": N, \"total_pages\": 1 }   // present ONLY on list endpoints\n}\n\nAuth model:\n- POST /login returns {accessToken, refreshToken} inside `data`. Tests save both.\n- POST /refresh exchanges a refresh token for a new access token (refresh is reused).\n- /student/** and /teacher/** require a Bearer ACCESS token (typ=access). Refresh tokens used here -> 401.\n- Postman Bearer Token auth references {{studentAccessToken}}/{{teacherAccessToken}} - paste raw JWT (no 'Bearer' prefix).\n\nFolders:\n1. Registration\n2. Login (saves access + refresh tokens from data)\n3. Refresh\n4. Student APIs (list endpoint includes pagination)\n5. Teacher APIs (search endpoint includes pagination)\n6. Negative (RBAC + auth + token-type mismatch)\n\nSetup:\n- gatewayUrl defaults to http://localhost:4000 (docker-compose). For K8s: http://<EC2-1>:30000.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 - Registration",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register student (role-scoped)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{gatewayUrl}}/register/student",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{studentEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{studentPassword}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created or 409 Conflict (already registered)', () => pm.expect([201, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('envelope code matches HTTP status', () => pm.expect(json.code).to.eql(String(pm.response.code)));",
                  "pm.test('no pagination on single-item response', () => pm.expect(json.pagination).to.be.undefined);",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  pm.test('data.role = student', () => pm.expect(json.data.role).to.eql('student'));",
                  "  pm.test('data.email matches input', () => pm.expect(json.data.email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('studentEmail')));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register teacher (role-scoped)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{gatewayUrl}}/register/teacher",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{teacherEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{teacherPassword}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created or 409 Conflict', () => pm.expect([201, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  pm.test('data.role = teacher', () => pm.expect(json.data.role).to.eql('teacher'));",
                  "}"
                ]
